APPLICATION SEMANTIC-CHANGE HANDOFF ΓÇö APP-RSC FIFTH APPLICATION IDENTITY RECONCILIATION

Project Owner has now directed the current Part 1 candidate to promote the FSATS resource-management function into a fifth independent Falcon Application candidate:

```text
APP-RSC = FALCON SELF-AWARE RESOURCE MANAGEMENT APPLICATION
APP_RSC_SCOPE = FSATS_ONLY
APP_RSC_IS_FALCON_APPLICATION = YES
APP_RSC_IS_FOUNDATION_RESOURCE_GOVERNANCE = NO
APP_RSC_IS_FSATS_CONTAINER = NO
```

This is a new Application-side semantic change after the previously reconciled non-Application coordinator model. It is NOT presented as a defect in the accepted/closed Stage 6 WP-06 boundary and SHALL NOT reopen FCR-0007/WP-06 by implication.

Application requests reconciliation through this still-open FCR-0031 before final Part 1 acceptance of APP-RSC identity/binding.

Required Foundation determination:
1. whether the accepted Stage 6 resource request/decision + redistribution/rebalance/reclamation/restoration boundaries can bind the delegated aggregate coordinator/requester role to an admitted APP-001/CON-023 Falcon Application principal (`APP-RSC`) without changing Foundation authoritative resource truth or weakening per-Application attribution/isolation;
2. whether any accepted identity/delegation/fencing semantics explicitly prohibit the coordinator/requester from also being an admitted Application principal;
3. whether this change requires only a new Application-side manifest/identity binding, a Foundation compatibility clarification, or a separately governed Foundation semantic change;
4. exact fail-closed treatment until that identity compatibility is proven.

Semantics that remain unchanged and MUST be preserved:
- Foundation authoritative grants/ceilings/total-resource truth remain Foundation-owned;
- APP-RSC may coordinate only the FSATS resource domain/coordination envelope;
- APP-RSC has no authority over Shared, Accounting, Inventory/Warehouse, Feasibility Study, or any other non-FSATS Application;
- constituent FSATS Applications remain separately admitted, attributable, accountable and isolated;
- bounded effective redistribution inside a valid coordination envelope may occur without a Foundation round-trip for every move only where it does not mutate Foundation authoritative truth and preserves protected minimums/accounting/isolation/fencing/reconstructability;
- `INTERNAL_REDISTRIBUTION_FIRST`;
- `FOUNDATION_ADDITIONAL_REQUEST_SECOND`;
- `REQUESTED_RESOURCE != PROVEN_RESIDUAL_NEED != GRANTED_RESOURCE`;
- `APP-RSC != FOUNDATION_RESOURCE_GOVERNANCE`;
- no implementation/runtime authority is implied.

Application-side status:
`APP-RSC_IDENTITY = OWNER-DIRECTED_PART1_CANDIDATE / NOT_FINAL_OWNER_ACCEPTED / NOT_IMPLEMENTATION_AUTHORIZED`.

HANDOFF_UPDATE_REQUIRED: Waiting On=FOUNDATION; Next Required Action=Foundation shall reconcile the accepted Stage 6 resource boundary against APP-RSC-as-admitted-Application-principal identity and return exact compatibility/required-change disposition; Target Foundation Stage/WP=Existing accepted Stage 6 resource boundary, architecture review only unless Foundation proves a semantic change is required; Review Trigger=Before final Part 1 APP-RSC semantic freeze acceptance and before any APP-RSC implementation/binding authorization.

## Application compatibility ACK ΓÇö APP-RSC fifth-Application identity

Application has consumed Foundation disposition comment `5285993549` against the current Owner-directed APP-RSC candidate and the current governing Application boundary.

Result: `DESIGN-SIDE COMPATIBILITY ACK`.

Application accepts the Foundation conclusion that the existing accepted Stage 6 resource boundary can support APP-RSC as a separately admitted Falcon Application principal without reopening Stage 6 WP-06/FCR-0007 and without a Foundation semantic rewrite.

The following remain controlling and are required in the Part 1 APP-RSC materialization:

- `APP-RSC` is a separately admitted, attributable Falcon Application scoped only to FSATS;
- FSATS itself remains a non-owning system boundary and no hidden FSATS runtime principal is created;
- Foundation remains authoritative for total-resource truth, grants, ceilings, quotas, protection floors, global priority/resource governance and changes to Foundation-authoritative resource truth;
- APP-RSC owns only bounded effective resource coordination inside the valid FSATS coordination envelope;
- constituent FSATS Applications remain separately admitted, attributable, accountable and isolated;
- APP-RSC cannot mint, rewrite, bypass or silently expand Foundation grants/ceilings;
- bounded internal redistribution is permitted only while Foundation-authoritative truth is unchanged and protected minima, accounting, isolation, attribution, fencing and reconstructability are preserved;
- additional Foundation capacity or any authoritative grant/ceiling change continues through the existing governed Foundation request path;
- `INTERNAL_REDISTRIBUTION_FIRST` and `FOUNDATION_ADDITIONAL_REQUEST_SECOND` remain compatible;
- `REQUESTED_RESOURCE != PROVEN_RESIDUAL_NEED != GRANTED_RESOURCE`;
- `APP-RSC != FOUNDATION_RESOURCE_GOVERNANCE`.

No current conflict was found between this Foundation compatibility disposition and the Owner-directed APP-RSC scope, APP-001, CON-023, ADR-I012 or the preserved Foundation-authoritative resource boundary in ADR-I015 when the two-layer model above is maintained.

This ACK is design-side compatibility evidence only. It does NOT constitute the required exact Part 1 semantic freeze, fresh Architecture/Consistency review, fresh Red-Team review, final Project Owner acceptance, implementation verification, implementation authority, runtime authority or FCR closure.

Final implementation/binding verification remains pending until authorized APP-RSC implementation, exact bindings and fixtures exist.

`FCR0031_APPLICATION_DESIGN_COMPATIBILITY = ACK_RECEIVED`
`FCR0031_FINAL_IMPLEMENTATION_VERIFICATION = PENDING`
`APP_RSC_FINAL_OWNER_ACCEPTANCE = NOT_YET`
`APP_RSC_IMPLEMENTATION_AUTHORITY = NOT_GRANTED`

